{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124372","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124372/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124372/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124372/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124372","id":5799224414,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHyaHlw","number":124372,"title":"Debugger: Add dual-channel protocol v2 for Godot 3.6","user":{"login":"nowasm","id":129167415,"node_id":"U_kgDOB7LwNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129167415?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm","html_url":"https://github.com/nowasm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"aaccff","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-11T08:01:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T09:44:47Z","closed_at":"2026-10-12T09:44:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124372","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124372","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124372.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124372.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n- Introduce a versioned, dual-channel debugger protocol for Godot 3.6, separating execution control from bounded output and inspection traffic.\n- Add acknowledged control commands, heartbeat/disconnect recovery, lazy paged variable inspection, and a matching built-in editor frontend.\n- Add black-box tests for pairing, stepping, reconnects, backpressure, variable paging, and editor behavior.\n\n## Motivation\nThe existing single-stream debugger became unreliable under high output and large paused-state payloads in a large GDScript project. The new control channel keeps step/continue responsive when data traffic is saturated.\n\n## Verification\n- Built from the current `3.6` branch on Windows with `scons platform=windows tools=yes target=release_debug -j8`.\n- Protocol/session model checks and all 9 black-box runtime scenarios passed against the newly built binary.\n- Built-in editor frontend smoke test completed 101 stops.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\n## Compatibility and review questions\nThis is a **draft** because the wire format intentionally replaces the existing Godot 3 remote debugger protocol. The built-in editor is updated, but unmodified external debugger clients will not attach. Maintainer guidance on an opt-in/legacy coexistence strategy is welcome before this is marked ready.\n\nThe companion VS Code client is proposed in [godot-vscode-plugin#1062](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-vscode-plugin/pull/1062). This PR targets `3.6` to match the tested implementation; I can retarget or split it if the project prefers `3.x` or another branch.\n\nRelated Godot 4.6 implementation: #124373.\n","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124372/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124372/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}